<title>NORWAY: Statoil awards Aasgard gasline contract.</title>
<headline>Statoil awards Aasgard gasline contract.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Den norske stats oljeselskap AS (Statoil) said on Thursday it had awarded a 895 million crown contract to lay a gas pipeline from the Aasgard field off mid-Norway to the Kaarstoe terminal north of Stavanger to U.S.-French group McDermott-ETPM West Inc.</p>
<p>Work on the 690-km line, which will have an annual capacity of 20 billion cubic metres of gas, is due to begin next spring and finish in autumn 1999. Operation will begin a year later.</p>
<p>Statoil said the contract was based on a frame agreement for laying submarine pipelines concluded between the two companies in 1995.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
